    badge: 'v1.1',

    whatTitle: 'What PISA is',
    whatBody:
      'PISA is the OECD Programme for International Student Assessment. It measures what students around 15 can apply in real contexts, not what they memorise. It runs every three years, computer-based in most countries, and it is not an OECD exam: it is a diagnostic assessment compared across countries.',
    whatS1: 'It measures competence, not syllabus',
    whatS1d:
      'The questions do not ask for a specific formula but for solving a problem set in the real world. The same skill can show up in a home budget or in public policy.',
    whatS2: 'Cyclic and comparable',
