    methodTitle: 'The PISAStyle v1.1 method',
    methodBody:
      'Every unit has three parts: a stimulus that sets the problem, one to two hours of study, and an assessment. Every item carries the eight mandatory fields of protocol v1.1 —domain, process, content, context, format, demand, level and anchor— plus an explanation of why that key and not another.',
    methodStep1: 'Stimulus',
    methodStep1d: 'The text or situation that gives context. It has to come from real life, not an abstract exercise.',
    methodStep2: '1–2 h of study',
    methodStep2d:
      'Directed work with the concepts and skills the stimulus demands. This is the part most people skip and the one that weighs most in the result.',
    methodStep3: 'Assessment',
    methodStep3d:
      'Items tagged by domain and level, with an explanation of each distractor. At the end you get a level estimate.',

    qualityTitle: 'Quality and limits',
    qualityBody:
      'Our validator requires every item to carry the eight protocol fields, an explanation of at least 80 characters and a cited source, and rejects duplicates, letter bias and predictable patterns. It is a filter on form, not on quality: it decides whether an item is well written, not whether it is pedagogically good. That judgement still belongs to a person.',
    whatNotTitle: 'What PISAStyle is not',
